  "slug": "protein-stable-07ab",
  "summary": "Three January 2026 GigaScience papers present knowledge-graph and annotation resources for plant, microbial, and Daphnia metabolomic data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is machine-readable integration of heterogeneous biological records into structures that can be queried. METRIN-KG joins plant metabolomes, trait data, and biotic interaction records within a knowledge graph exposed through an interactive search interface. KG-Microbe provides a modular construction framework that harmonizes bacterial and archaeal data and supports customizable taxa subsets. The Daphnia magna entry addresses an upstream step: deep metabolome annotation that combines multi-platform MS and NMR data with a Galaxy pipeline of more than 30 tools, yielding 8,181 annotated metabolites. Its output is an annotated compound inventory rather than a graph, so it does not share the graph-construction method of the other two entries. What is new in this set is the pairing of graph-based integration with workflow-level metabolite annotation for a specific ecotoxicological organism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-25"
}
